Q: Apache SSL error - Unable to configure server certificate for stapling A: <p>This seems to be bug that where the fix still hasn't made its way to the latest environments. I have the same problem. Here's my environment:</p>

<p>Server version: Apache/2.4.41
OS: Ubuntu 18.04</p>

<p>As a workaround, you can edit <code>ports.conf</code> so that the last listen directive is for a non-SSL port, i.e. <code>Listen 80</code>. Here's the whole file:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;IfModule ssl_module&gt;
    Listen 443 https
&lt;/IfModule&gt;

&lt;IfModule mod_gnutls.c&gt;
    Listen 443
&lt;/IfModule&gt;

Listen 80
</code></pre>

<p>And the problem is gone.</p>
